.\" man/man3/TreeSitter::Parser.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "TreeSitter::Parser" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "treesitter 0.1.0" "treesitter API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
TreeSitter::Parser \- Parses UTF\-8 text with one \fB\%Language\fR into a \fB\%Tree\fR.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "treesitter"\fR
.sp
\fBclass TreeSitter::Parser\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Parses UTF\-8 text with one \fB\%Language\fR into a \fB\%Tree\fR. Passing the previous tree, edited with \fB\%Tree#edit\fR, makes
the parse incremental. A parser is not safe to share between threads; use one per fiber that parses.
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.new(language : Language)\fR
A parser for \fIlanguage\fR; raises \fB\%Error\fR when the library rejects the grammar.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef included_regions=(regions : Array(Region)) : Array(Region)\fR
Limits the following parses to \fIregions\fR, in text order and not overlapping, as for a language embedded in
another one\(aqs text; an empty array parses everything again. Raises \fB\%Error\fR when the library rejects them.
.TP 4
\fBdef language : Language\fR
The grammar in use.
.TP 4
\fBdef language=(language : Language) : Language\fR
Switches the grammar; raises \fB\%Error\fR when the library rejects it.
.TP 4
\fBdef parse(text : String, old_tree : Tree | Nil = nil) : Tree\fR
Parses \fItext\fR, reusing the unchanged parts of \fIold_tree\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef parse(old_tree : Tree | Nil = nil, &read : Int32 \-> Bytes) : Tree\fR
Parses text read in chunks: the block gets a byte offset and returns the bytes from there (any length, an empty
slice at the end). Each chunk must stay unchanged until the next call; the parser keeps the last one alive.
.TP 4
\fBdef parse(old_tree : Tree | Nil, *, cancel : Int32 \-> Bool, &read : Int32 \-> Bytes) : Tree | Nil\fR
Parses like \fB\%parse(old_tree, \%&read)\fR, asking \fIcancel\fR with the byte reached as it goes; returns \fB\%nil\fR when
\fIcancel\fR returned \fB\%true\fR, and the next parse starts over.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/tree_sitter/parser.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "TreeSitter" (3cr),
